{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43788576",
      "title": "Working with Outputs & Emitting Data",
      "lectureOrder": 35,
      "videoOrder": 31,
      "sourceHash": "9f3f8839c6848c6e4d65485c4bdaea20b4f705f09864712aa1744df97352a749",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.36,
          "end": 2.1,
          "en": "To set up such a property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 4.77,
          "en": "you can add another regular property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.77,
          "end": 7.08,
          "en": "and give it any name of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.08,
          "end": 8.7,
          "en": "For example, select",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 8.7,
          "end": 13.23,
          "en": "because we wanna create kind of a custom select event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.23,
          "end": 14.22,
          "en": "you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.22,
          "end": 16.68,
          "en": "We wanna pass the information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 16.68,
          "end": 20.58,
          "en": "that a specific user was selected to the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.58,
          "end": 23.13,
          "en": "that's using the UserComponent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.13,
          "end": 25.98,
          "en": "So select sounds like a fitting name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.98,
          "end": 28.98,
          "en": "And this select component must be decorated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 28.98,
          "end": 32.67,
          "en": "with another decorator that's imported from Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.67,
          "end": 34.893,
          "en": "the Output decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.36,
          "end": 38.91,
          "en": "This is imported from @angular/core",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.91,
          "end": 41.31,
          "en": "and then used just like input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.31,
          "end": 45.123,
          "en": "by executing it like this in front of the select property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.71,
          "end": 48.72,
          "en": "Now, unlike an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.72,
          "end": 52.5,
          "en": "the select property will receive an initial value though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.5,
          "end": 54.423,
          "en": "assigned with that equal sign.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.5,
          "end": 60.5,
          "en": "And that initial value is a new EventEmitter object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.99,
          "end": 64.86,
          "en": "where EventEmitter is actually also imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.86,
          "end": 66.663,
          "en": "from @angular/core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.46000000000001,
          "end": 70.62,
          "en": "And this instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.62,
          "end": 73.89,
          "en": "of the EventEmitter class we're creating here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.89,
          "end": 77.82,
          "en": "so this EventEmitter object we're getting here in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.82,
          "end": 82.59,
          "en": "will then allow us to emit custom values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.59,
          "end": 84.66,
          "en": "through that select property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.66,
          "end": 87.783,
          "en": "to any parent component that's interested.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.89,
          "end": 92.94,
          "en": "And for that, here in onSelectUser, which is that function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.94,
          "end": 95.09,
          "en": "that's triggered when we click that button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96,
          "end": 98.82,
          "en": "in that function, in this method here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.82,
          "end": 101.25,
          "en": "I want to use this select property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.25,
          "end": 103.893,
          "en": "to emit a new value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.03,
          "end": 107.55,
          "en": "And now we just have to pass the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.55,
          "end": 111.15,
          "en": "that should be emitted to this emit method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.15,
          "end": 113.88,
          "en": "which is provided by that EventEmitter object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.88,
          "end": 115.743,
          "en": "which is stored in select.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.03,
          "end": 121.71,
          "en": "Now, we don't have to set a value here if we don't want to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.71,
          "end": 124.38,
          "en": "but we, of course, can.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.38,
          "end": 126.27,
          "en": "And we might, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.27,
          "end": 129.48,
          "en": "want to accept another input first,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.48,
          "end": 134.48,
          "en": "the ID of the user, let's say, which should also be a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.86,
          "end": 138.9,
          "en": "because in my dummy users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.9,
          "end": 142.053,
          "en": "every user has such a string ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 143.01,
          "end": 146.31,
          "en": "and that should also be required.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.31,
          "end": 148.23,
          "en": "And then we can convince TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 148.23,
          "end": 150.393,
          "en": "with that exclamation mark that it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 151.38,
          "end": 156.38,
          "en": "And now we could emit this.id here in onSelectUser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156.48,
          "end": 158.25,
          "en": "because we receive it as an input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 158.25,
          "end": 159.81,
          "en": "and we pass it back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 159.81,
          "end": 163.653,
          "en": "to the parent component whenever a user is selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 164.57999999999998,
          "end": 167.13,
          "en": "Now we have to go back to the app.component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 167.13,
          "end": 169.95,
          "en": "and of course, set the ID here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 169.95,
          "end": 174.90699999999998,
          "en": "and set it to users[0].id on the first user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 175.95,
          "end": 179.7,
          "en": "and then copy and paste this to all other users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 179.7,
          "end": 183.273,
          "en": "and access the other indexes of those users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.5,
          "end": 187.35,
          "en": "And I'll now press that format document shortcut",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 187.35,
          "end": 189.573,
          "en": "to make this code look a bit prettier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 191.25,
          "end": 194.873,
          "en": "And we can now also listen to our custom event here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 194.873,
          "end": 197.73,
          "en": "because that's the other thing we added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 197.73,
          "end": 200.04,
          "en": "We added this select output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 200.04,
          "end": 201.54,
          "en": "and with that added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 201.54,
          "end": 206.54,
          "en": "we can use event binding on our custom component to listen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 206.64,
          "end": 210,
          "en": "for this select event because we, in the end now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 210,
          "end": 213.78300000000002,
          "en": "did create our own custom event called select.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 215.1,
          "end": 216.48,
          "en": "And we can now handle this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 216.48,
          "end": 220.47,
          "en": "just as we can handle any built-in event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 220.47,
          "end": 224.28,
          "en": "We can add a method to the app.component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 224.28,
          "end": 226.03,
          "en": "which could be called onSelectUser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 227.43,
          "end": 229.563,
          "en": "The name, of course, is up to you though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 231.32999999999998,
          "end": 235.863,
          "en": "And here we then expect to get the ID of that user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 237.24,
          "end": 240.06,
          "en": "Now, if I just add the ID parameter like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 240.06,
          "end": 243.18,
          "en": "I'm again getting a complaint by TypeScript though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 243.18,
          "end": 247.77,
          "en": "because the parameter 'id' implicitly has the 'any' type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 247.77,
          "end": 251.16,
          "en": "So that's a similar problem as we faced before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 251.16,
          "end": 252.63,
          "en": "because in the end, the problem here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 252.63,
          "end": 255.45,
          "en": "is that TypeScript doesn't know which type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 255.45,
          "end": 258.12,
          "en": "of value will get here and it wants to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 258.12,
          "end": 261,
          "en": "because it is its main thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 261,
          "end": 265.59,
          "en": "Therefore, just as before with those properties here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 265.59,
          "end": 268.26,
          "en": "we have to tell TypeScript which kind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 268.26,
          "end": 271.86,
          "en": "of value will be received here in this method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 271.86,
          "end": 273.63,
          "en": "by adding a colon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 273.63,
          "end": 276.35,
          "en": "and by then adding the type that will get here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 276.35,
          "end": 278.103,
          "en": "in this case, a string type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 279.06,
          "end": 281.46,
          "en": "And now with that, TypeScript is happy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 281.46,
          "end": 282.78,
          "en": "And here for the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 282.78,
          "end": 287.7,
          "en": "we can simply console.log selected user with id",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 287.7,
          "end": 289.44,
          "en": "and then output that ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 289.44,
          "end": 292.14300000000003,
          "en": "that we're receiving, like this, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 293.94,
          "end": 297.65999999999997,
          "en": "Now with that added, it's this onSelectUser method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 297.65999999999997,
          "end": 299.55,
          "en": "which I wanna set as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 299.55,
          "end": 302.763,
          "en": "for my custom select event, like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 303.99,
          "end": 306,
          "en": "However, now, of course, I'm getting an error here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 306,
          "end": 310.47,
          "en": "because onSelectUser expected one argument but got zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 310.47,
          "end": 314.01,
          "en": "I am not passing anything here yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 314.01,
          "end": 318.12,
          "en": "And the value I do wanna pass here to onSelectUser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 318.12,
          "end": 322.05,
          "en": "of course, should be the ID that is emitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 322.05,
          "end": 323.823,
          "en": "by this user component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 324.96,
          "end": 328.41,
          "en": "But how do we now get hold of that emitted value here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 328.41,
          "end": 330.363,
          "en": "in the template of the app.component?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 331.38,
          "end": 335.25,
          "en": "Well, you can get hold of emitted values with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 335.25,
          "end": 339.21,
          "en": "of a special variable that's provided by Angular:",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 339.21,
          "end": 341.763,
          "en": "the $event variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 342.78,
          "end": 344.01,
          "en": "That's a reserved name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 344.01,
          "end": 348.93,
          "en": "It's a variable provided by Angular in its templates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 348.93,
          "end": 351.57,
          "en": "or specifically in the parts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 351.57,
          "end": 355.29,
          "en": "where you handle events in your templates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 355.29,
          "end": 357.42,
          "en": "So for example, here between the quotes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 357.42,
          "end": 359.58,
          "en": "of this event binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 359.58,
          "end": 364.58,
          "en": "and this $event variable will then hold the data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 364.74,
          "end": 367.32,
          "en": "the value that was emitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 367.32,
          "end": 369.423,
          "en": "by the event you're listening to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 371.01,
          "end": 374.07,
          "en": "And with that, we therefore then are able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 374.07,
          "end": 375.963,
          "en": "to handle that event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 376.95,
          "end": 380.13,
          "en": "And now, of course, we can copy and paste that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 380.13,
          "end": 384.273,
          "en": "to all the other app-user components as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 385.29,
          "end": 388.89,
          "en": "And with that done, if we save everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 388.89,
          "end": 391.71,
          "en": "and we open those developer tools here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 391.71,
          "end": 394.71,
          "en": "if I click on a user, you see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 394.71,
          "end": 399.39,
          "en": "that I get this output selected with user id u1.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 399.39,
          "end": 403.26,
          "en": "For the second user, I get u2 and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 403.26,
          "end": 406.77,
          "en": "So this is working and this, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 406.77,
          "end": 410.76,
          "en": "is how you can emit your own events with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 410.76,
          "end": 414.09000000000003,
          "en": "of output and how you can then handle them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 414.09000000000003,
          "end": 417.093,
          "en": "and also get access to the emitted data.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
